Compare two designs:

```java
// Design 1
class Car {
    private final Engine engine;
    Car() { this.engine = new Engine(); }
}

// Design 2
class Car {
    private Driver driver;
    void assignDriver(Driver driver) { this.driver = driver; }
}
```

Assume these are explicit *modeling policies*, not conclusions drawn from Java field syntax alone: in Design 1, Car exclusively owns its internally constructed Engine as a lifecycle-dependent part (it is never shared, transferred or exposed); in Design 2, Driver is independently owned, can be assigned to other cars, and outlives any particular Car reference. Under those assumptions, which statement best describes the two relationships?
